User: You are tasked with implementing a function to balance a string containing various types of grouping symbols. The grouping symbols include parentheses '()', square brackets '[]', and curly braces '{}'. The function should determine if the input string has balanced grouping symbols and return true if it does, and false otherwise.

The function signature is:
```cpp
bool isBalanced(const std::string& input);
```

For the purpose of this problem, a string is considered balanced if each opening symbol has a corresponding closing symbol and they are properly nested. For example, the string "([]{})" is balanced, while "([)]" is not.

You should implement the function `isBalanced` to determine if the input string has balanced grouping symbols and return true if it does, and false otherwise.
Assistant:
```cpp
#include <stack>
#include <string>

bool isBalanced(const std::string& input) {
    std::stack<char> stack;
    for (char c : input) {
        if (c == '(' || c == '[' || c == '{') {
            stack.push(c);
        } else if (c == ')' || c == ']' || c == '}') {
            if (stack.empty()) {
                return false;  // Unmatched closing symbol
            }
            char open = stack.top();
            stack.pop();
            if ((c == ')' && open != '(') ||
                (c == ']' && open != '[') ||
                (c == '}' && open != '{')) {
                return false;  // Mismatched opening and closing symbols
            }
        }
    }
    return stack.empty();  // Return true if stack is empty, false otherwise
}
```

